# Per-expert dispatch framework: routing-aware expert execution with
# the fused GEMV path bypassed entirely (campaign: sub4bit-vram-kernel).
#
# Design:   docs/design-routing-aware-expert-execution.md
# Campaign: docs/campaigns/sub4bit-vram-kernel.md
# Gate:     a model with >= 512 experts serves on one card with routing-aware
#           expert execution: only the routed experts computed per token.
#
# This is the DISPATCH FRAMEWORK only — the per-expert OCL kernel that makes
# this path fast is a separate patch. With this patch alone, per-expert
# dispatch routes all routed experts through the existing CPU tier
# (moe_cpu_expert, patch 0011), proving the dispatch mechanism is correct
# before the GPU kernel exists.
#
# The mechanism: when per-expert dispatch is active, try_acquire_simultaneous
# marks ALL routed experts as CPU-tier misses (kCpuTierSentinelSlot). The
# fused GEMV kernels (mlp_gate_up, mlp_down) see all sentinels and skip every
# work-group. dispatch_cpu_tier() computes each routed expert on the host.
# cpu_tier_join() writes the results to scratch.y. mlp_reduce() runs
# unchanged.
#
# This proves two things (the campaign's red-first cells):
#   1. The fused path is refused when per-expert dispatch is active.
#   2. An unrouted expert is never computed — dispatch_cpu_tier() receives
#      exactly the unique experts from the router's top-k, never num_expert.
#
# Applied against the pinned runtime, build 2026.4.0-22849-71640275d29, on
# top of patches/0003-0037.
#
# What changes:
#   properties.hpp                New property: moe_per_expert_dispatch (bool,
#                                  RW, default false).
#   options.inl                   OV_CONFIG_RELEASE_OPTION registration.
#   compiled_model.cpp            PropertyName entry (RO at compiled time).
#   plugin.cpp                    PropertyName entry (RW at plugin level).
#   expert_weight_providers.hpp   OffloadExpertWeightProvider:
#                                  _per_expert_dispatch flag + setter.
#   expert_weight_providers.cpp   try_acquire_simultaneous: when
#                                  _per_expert_dispatch is set, ALL experts
#                                  go to cpu_tier_misses as sentinels.
#   moe_3gemm_swiglu_opt.cpp     _per_expert_dispatch flag wired from the
#                                  new MOE_PER_EXPERT_DISPATCH config property.
#   moe_otd_perf.hpp             New counter: per_expert_dispatches.
#   moe_otd_runtime.cpp          Print per_expert_dispatches in dump().
#   moe_3gemm_gpu_test.cpp       Red-first test:
#                                  per-expert dispatch counter exists and
#                                  increments correctly.
#
# Fable review (3 findings, all fixed):
#   1. CONFIRMED: _per_expert_dispatch missing from make_deep_copy clone
#      field list — the executing impl always had it false. Fixed: added
#      cur_moe->_per_expert_dispatch = _per_expert_dispatch after _cpu_gate_act.
#   2. PLAUSIBLE: _per_expert_dispatch set from config unconditionally, even
#      when the weight provider is not offloaded. Fixed: guarded behind
#      _weight_provider->is_offloaded() — stays false on a fully-resident model.
#   3. PLAUSIBLE: no assertion that cpu_tier_misses is empty on entry to the
#      per-expert dispatch early-return path (asymmetric with resident provider).
#      Fixed: added OPENVINO_ASSERT(cpu_tier_misses->empty(), ...).
#

